KEY LIFT PENALTIES
n=11: direct c=11 lift costs 2.533e+07 times a c=2 lift for fixed input set (paper avoids it by the odd-prime polynomial method).
n=12: paper uses composite lift chain x2,x2,x2,x2,x3,x3; certificate clock C=23 is prime, so the repo unit-shell residual is 0.
n=13: direct c=13 lift costs 5.688e+09 times a c=2 lift for fixed input set (paper avoids it by the odd-prime polynomial method).

THM-398 DODGE-FIRST FILTER
n  dominance cut       all-short cap at v=n   n-clock safe gap   gap/cap
11 v > 10*max(other)              0.016529           0.074380      4.50
12 v > 11*max(other)              0.013889           0.069444      5.00
13 v > 12*max(other)              0.011834           0.065089      5.50
   General interval criterion: for any chosen runner v, a component of G(S\{v}) longer than 2/(n*v) certifies looseness.
   For a multiple v=n*w, the only residual is all-short: every component of G(S\{v}) has length <= 2/(n^2*w).

