   Sampled all-short tight cases: 0 for every listed n.

INTERPRETATION
- Paper exactness is prime-fiber exactness: certify J(k,p)=empty for many p.
- Repo clocks ask for a proof quotient first: n-clock, C=2n-1 shells, pair pinches, D/U/N owners.
- THM-398 inserts an interval oracle before the quotient scan: long safe components dodge any one runner.
- S573 identifies n|v as the Vitali handoff; the fallback is arc alignment, not ordinary tuple search.
- If the certificate quotient is complete, the expensive object is not p^k tuples but at most a few thousand shell/fiber rows plus O(k^2) pair tests.
- n=12 is the clearest rotated case: paper n=12 is composite, but C=23 is prime, so every antipodal shell is a unit shell.
